body:
On an idle entity, with no Stream Input bound and no Stream Output streaming, a SET_CONFIGURATION whose configuration_index equals the current configuration answers SUCCESS. It then also sends an unsolicited SET_CONFIGURATION response to every registered controller.

The engine's own design says it should not. In `hdl/aecp/ucode/gen_ucode.py`, the E_SCFG micro-program compares the commanded index with the current one after SEND_RESP and skips NOTIFY_ENQ when they are equal. Milan v1.2 5.4.5.2, first paragraph: after a successful response to one of the commands in [ATDECC 7.5.2], the PAAD-AE sends an unsolicited notification only "if the command modifies the state", and then to all registered controllers except the requesting one. A no-change SET_CONFIGURATION modifies nothing. IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.4.7 alone says "On success this command also sends an unsolicited notification"; Milan's 5.4.5.2 narrows that rule for a PAAD-AE.

Observed on silicon at processor `2cbed0a9`: SET_CONFIGURATION(0) on the single configuration 0 answered SUCCESS (cdl 16, index 0), followed by an unsolicited response (u=1, index 0) to the registered controller.

The case is reachable only on an idle bench. While streams are bound, Milan v1.2 5.4.2.5 refuses SET_CONFIGURATION with STREAM_IS_RUNNING first.

Done when:
- a SET_CONFIGURATION to the current index answers SUCCESS without any unsolicited notification;
- a real change still notifies once;
- a suite case covers both, each with a planted mutant;
- the processor suites and the parent consumer gates pass.
